<title>UK: UK sets plan for new 600-place PFI prison.</title>
<headline>UK sets plan for new 600-place PFI prison.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new 600-place prison is to be built at Marchington, Staffordshire under the Private Finance Initiative, Britain's Prison Service said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the facility, housing Category B and C prisoners, will include a 200-place community therapeutic regime.</p>
<p>The Service would have the option to raise the capacity to 800 prisoners if necessary.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
